799333710259603 -id    video I wanna see this just because The Room (and Tommy Wiseau) is fascinating in just how awful it is and I want a movie about what went on behind the scenes. This is based on the memoirs of one of the film's actors.   However, a little ambivalent about James Franco's performance here. He doesn't quite hit the mark. Granted, there are times when it is best to avoid making your performance come off as a mere impression or parody. I'll probably end up seeing this regardless, but it doesn't feel as spot-on as I'd like.  I am also kind of interested to see if the Franco/Rogen duo can pull off something that's not completely lowbrow (I mean, they did do that one movie about their friend that had cancer, but if I recall they had limited roles in the film and off screen were responsible for only part of the script). 066d3d31-8ab5-4f43-f765-08d5b52ea2a6
